WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:05.520
The filmmakers responsible for the MCU knew
Thanos was coming long before we did.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:09.830
There are moments throughout Marvel's movies
that go by in the blink of an eye, but are

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:13.820
actually very important to the big picture
- we just didn't know it yet.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.900
Here’s your Spoilers ahead!

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.520
Warning we are saying what’s important to
Endgame - we think - but we aren’t spoiling

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.480
specific plot points to Endgame.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.500
We’re just using the clues from past films.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:31.020
So you’re safe... unless we’re right about
everything, and if so… oops!

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:37.240
It's an easy thing to forget: Behind his high-tech
armor and sarcastic facade, Tony Stark is

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.220
still only human.

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:41.640
He's not physically the strongest of the Avengers
that would be the Hulk, obviously — but

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.300
Stark certainly has the strongest personality.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.320
"Security breach..."

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:48.840
“Phil! Come in.”

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:49.560
"Phil?"

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:50.960
"I can't stay."

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.440
"His first name is Agent."

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:57.680
Tony Stark's plucky personality makes it easy
to forget that he's ultimately fallible.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:02.680
Rather than being all wit and one-liners,
Tony struggles with a feeling of powerlessness

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:06.910
after the Battle of New York, and it's a feeling
that we would never have associated with such

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:07.960
a powerful figure.

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:13.220
In Iron Man 3, Tony has flashbacks to the
black maw of the wormhole that he never thought

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:13.760
he'd come out of.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:19.120
His knowledge of the reality of what's out
there in space especially civilizations with

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:24.480
bigger, badder weapons haunts him, plaguing
him with PTSD flashbacks and nightmares.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:30.400
In Avengers: Age of Ultron, this fear of the
danger lurking in space manifests in the nightmarish

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.080
hallucinations that Scarlet Witch subjects
him to.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:38.720
Tony sees Black Widow, Cap, Thor… all of
his friends... broken and dead.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.920
"You… couldn't…

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:44.860
save… us.."

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.400
In a way, this turns out to be a vision of
the future.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:53.740
In Infinity War, as hard as he tries, Tony
is unable to stop Thanos from getting the

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:56.180
final Infinity Stone needed for the big Snap.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:01.440
He watches in horror as his friends fall around
him, while he stands powerless.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:06.140
We probably can't convince you to watch Thor:
The Dark World if you haven't already.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:09.820
And if you have watched it, a single viewing
is probably enough.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:14.850
The plot is a tangled web, and Thor is honestly
kind of insufferable.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:16.920
"At least pretend to enjoy yourself."

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:21.740
But while The Dark World is among the weakest
entries in the Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:26.680
the movie does a phenomenal job of introducing
the nature of the Infinity Stones and teasing

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:27.860
their future importance.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:33.150
Thor and his girlfriend, Dr. Jane Foster,
are thrown into an age-old conflict between

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:34.660
Asgard and the Dark Elves.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:39.400
Long ago, the elves had sought to conquer
the Nine Realms with the power of the Aether,

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.460
a red-tinged force created from the Reality
Stone.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:47.750
It was sealed away by Odin's own father, but
it was unleashed when the Nine Realms aligned.

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:49.480
Then, it infected Jane.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:54.010
They're only able to destroy the Aether when
it's fused with Malekith, the leader of the

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:56.380
Dark Elves, but the Reality Stone remains.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.320
In a post-credit scene, it's officially called
an Infinity Stone:

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:02.920
"The Tesseract is already on Asgard.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:07.060
It's not wise to keep two Infinity Stones
close together."

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:12.580
Because Asgard is already guarding the Space
Stone, they send the Reality Stone to the

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:16.380
Collector, who we find out has his own goal
of collecting them all.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.900
Being a superhero isn't your average nine-to-five.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:25.210
You have to fight bad guys all over the world,
face down death on countless occasions, and

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:28.560
deal with overpowered co-workers who have
anger issues.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:30.600
We're looking at you, Hulk.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.860
Keeping all that in mind, there's a good reason
why the Avengers aren't really the sort of

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:39.360
people to settle down and start families…
except, of course for Hawkeye.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:44.920
Clint Barton lives a double life: out in the
world, he's a deadly archer and agent of SHIELD.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:47.360
But at home, he's a husband and father..

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:52.320
In Avengers: Age of Ultron, Clint surprised
everyone by taking them to his homestead and

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.760
safe house, where his wife and kids live.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:58.960
That's where he was holed up under house arrest
during the events of Infinity War, which explains

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.280
his notable absence from the film's posters.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.780
Now, do you know what a Checkov’s [check-off’s]
Gun is?

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:08.420
Basically if a gun appears in act one someone
should get shot in act 2.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:13.380
Well… there’s a reason Clint’s family
was all smiles in Age Of Ultron and every

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:16.500
trailer for Endgame showed an Angry “Ronin”
style Clint Barton.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:18.120
Do the math....

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:23.040
Wakanda may be an isolated nation that hides
its secrets from the world, but that doesn't

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:25.860
mean we hadn't heard about it before Black
Panther.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:31.180
Wakanda previously refused aid from other
countries, and its people rarely venture outside

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:31.720
of its borders.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:37.330
That's why it's a huge international incident
when civilians, including Wakandan scientists

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:42.470
on a goodwill mission, are killed in the crossfire
between the Avengers and Crossbones' terrorist

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:45.140
crew at the beginning of Captain America:
Civil War.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:48.360
"Our people's blood is spilled on foreign
soil."

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:53.600
Captain America's shield is made from the
strongest material in the world: vibranium.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:59.070
As a former weapons manufacturer, Tony Stark
is well aware that Wakanda is the only one

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:00.620
place you can get vibranium.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:05.300
It's highly valued on the black market, where
disreputable arms dealers like Ulysses Klaue

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:05.940
[KLAW] operate.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:11.051
We meet Klaue just before he loses an arm
during an encounter with Ultron in Age of

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:11.600
Ultron.

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:16.860
When we see him again in Black Panther, he's
replaced the appendage with a robotic prosthesis,

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:20.340
which makes him all the more dangerous…
or at least more badass.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:25.420
The MCU was packed with references to Wakanda
long before we ever saw the place for ourselves

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:26.800
in Black Panther.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:31.040
Tony Stark and Steve Rogers don't always get
along.

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:35.120
In fact, it's their disagreements that ultimately
tear the Avengers in two.

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:36.280
"You've been busy."

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:37.800
"And you've been a complete idiot.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:41.900
But that doesn't mean they're not friends,
and friends always have each other's best

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.060
interests at heart.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:47.860
During the events of Captain America: Civil
War, that's what divides Iron Man and Captain

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:52.360
America: each man thinks he knows what's right
for their super-powered friends.

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:56.400
Fast-forward to the end of the movie, after
they're been able to punch the ever-loving

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:58.860
heck out of one other and feel a little better.

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:02.180
Despite their many differences, they still
support one another.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:07.740
Tony receives a package, and inside is a cell
phone and a letter, which reads in part:

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:09.080
"We all need family.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:12.020
The Avengers are yours.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:13.860
Maybe more so than mine."

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:18.020
It's the line about family that weighs heavily
on Tony's future.

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:23.400
The post-credit scene shows a young Peter
Parker experimenting with web shooters, and

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:27.120
in the following films we see that Spider-Man
is something of an adopted son to Tony.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:32.740
Cap's words resonate even further considering
the conversation Tony and Pepper have in Infinity

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:33.280
War.

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:36.540
“Last night, I dreamt that we had a kid.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:38.220
It was so real."

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:40.660
We all need family… right?

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:47.729
After the big Snap, and after countless worlds
start crumbling into dust, the Mad Titan himself

00:06:47.729 --> 00:06:52.900
is taken to a red-tinged plane where nothing
exists, save for a familiar-looking arch and

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:54.200
the silhouette of a little girl.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:59.320
It's Gamora — the same young Gamora that
Thanos met when he killed half the people

00:06:59.400 --> 00:06:59.940
on her planet.

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:02.360
She asks him what his victory cost.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:06.820
Not looking the least bit triumphant, Thanos
grimly replies:

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:08.520
"Everything."

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.580
But what does that mean?

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:15.740
Of course the scene emphasizes the fact that
Thanos really did love Gamora, but the moment

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:17.700
is about more than mere reminiscence.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:22.980
In order to get the Soul Stone, Thanos had
to sacrifice the soul of somebody he loved.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:27.040
He sacrificed Gamora, and her soul was claimed
by the Stone.

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:32.380
With the power of the Infinity Stones, Thanos
wiped out exactly half the population of the

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:33.120
whole universe.

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:37.520
All those souls have to go somewhere — in
the Marvel universe, anyway.

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:40.820
They go to the Soul World, a pocket dimension
in the Soul Stone itself.

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:41.340
So…

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:45.080
Gamora’s in the Soul Stone, that what it
meant, right?

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:47.480
That might be important later.

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:53.860
When the first Thor film was released in 2011,
magic still wasn't a part of the Marvel Cinematic

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:55.420
Universe only science.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:08:00.860
Sure, Tony Stark made a flying metal suit
and an artificial intelligence so smart that

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:05.580
it could backtalk, but that wasn't actual
magic just good old-fashioned engineering.

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:08.580
Well, Thor changed all that… sort of.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:14.380
In a rather romantic scene with Dr. Jane Foster,
Thor explains that what people call "magic"

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:17.080
is the same thing as science back where he
comes from.

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:22.900
Norse mythology interprets the Nine Realms
as branches of the world tree, Yggdrasil,

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:25.320
but we would think of them as planets.

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:27.060
"Hahaha…

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.100
… Tell me more."

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:36.430
The rainbow bridge Bifrost creates wormholes
in which Asgardians travel, and Asgardians

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:37.040
aren't gods.

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:41.880
They're a super-powered race of aliens who
just so happen to look a lot like humans.

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:46.660
We didn't know it back then, but this explanation
paves the way for other planets and other

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:49.200
civilizations to come into play in the MCU.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:55.420
Asgardians were the first alien species introduced
in the MCU, but later films would add the

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:57.800
Chitauri, the Kree, and the Skrulls, to name
but a few.

00:08:59.529 --> 00:09:04.580
In some form, The Tesseract has shown up in
a number of Marvel films, serving as the MacGuffin

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:06.700
in not one, but three movies.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:11.380
In Captain America, we learn that it was originally
brought to Earth by Asgard, only to be stolen

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:13.380
by Nazis and HYDRA.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:18.740
In Captain Marvel, it was given to Project
PEGASUS by Howard Stark with the goal of making

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:19.960
a lightspeed engine.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:25.490
It was stolen by Loki in The Avengers… only
to be taken back to Asgard and stolen again

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:27.320
by Loki in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:31.080
But another Infinity stone had been hiding
in plain sight.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:36.540
Loki's scepter is special for a reason, and
not just because it's the season's must-have

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:39.520
accessory that perfectly matches his horned
helmet.

00:09:40.009 --> 00:09:44.379
Gifted to Loki by Thanos, the scepter isn't
just any old alien weapon.

00:09:44.379 --> 00:09:48.920
It actually contains the Mind Stone, which
is why it can be used for mind-control and

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:50.060
general evildoing.

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:55.800
Once Loki is carted away in chains to Asgard,
SHIELD studies the scepter and is able to

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.640
discern that it had some kind of connection
to the Tesseract.

00:09:59.129 --> 00:10:03.860
Then it's stolen by HYDRA and used to give
powers to test subjects like Scarlet Witch

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:04.760
and Quicksilver.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:09.529
When the Avengers get their hands on it again,
Tony Stark and Bruce Banner discover that

00:10:09.529 --> 00:10:11.900
within the scepter… something is thinking.

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:18.460
"I mean this could be a… it's not a human
mind, but…I mean, look at this."

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:23.900
Yes, it's the Mind Stone, which is then used
to create Vision in order to keep the power

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:24.620
away from Ultron.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:26.360
Got that?

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:26.880
Good!

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:32.100
Let's not forget how important the Guardians
of the Galaxy series has been in tying together

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:34.060
the plotline of the Infinity Stones.

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:39.300
Despite taking place far, far away from Earth,
the films have introduced key players and

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:41.160
background in the struggle for the Stones.

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:46.580
What's also important to note is that Guardians
of the Galaxy Vol. 2 may have introduced the

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:49.040
most powerful character in the whole MCU.

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:50.660
Nope…

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:52.300
We're not talking about Ego.

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:57.940
His power pales in comparison to the mighty
force cocooned in golden pipes by the Sovereign.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:03.280
The second Guardians of the Galaxy film starts
with Rocket doing what he does best stealing.

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:05.400
And stealing batteries, no less.

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:07.000
"What were you thinking?"

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:09.610
"Dude, they were really easy to steal."

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:10.300
"That's your defense?"

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:10.840
"Come on."

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:15.660
This draws the wrath of the Sovereign, who
make it their mission to destroy the Guardians.

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:20.300
Failing to do so by more conventional means
prompts the Sovereign leader, High Priestess

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:26.560
Ayesha, to create a new weapon: a new being,
more powerful, more beautiful, and more capable

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:28.040
of destroying the Guardians.

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:30.220
She decides to name it Adam.

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:35.259
And comic readers already know: Adam Warlock
is one of the most powerful characters in

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:36.160
Marvel's comics.

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:41.020
Rocket's sticky fingers may have lead to the
creation of the most powerful being in the

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:41.840
universe.

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:43.060
"Uh-huh."

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:46.060
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:49.160
Plus, even more Looper videos about the MCU
are coming soon.

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:53.700
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

